mong Healthcare peers. Each employee generates $13K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Cresco Labs Inc. is a micro-cap healthcare business with a $185M market cap on $656M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -9% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -19.1pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 50%.","The business throws off $38M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 18.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -19.1pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Price sits 152% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.522007212653615},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can 